{title: Quiet and Peaceful}
{subtitle: 1 Chronicles 4:4; 4:18; 8:31; 9:37; Joshua 15:58; 1 Chronicles 4:39–40}
{key: D}
{tempo: 82}
{time: 4/4}

{comment: Intro}
| [D] | [D] | [D] | [D] |
| [D] |

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
Penuel was the father of Gedor
[G]Ezer the father of Hus[A]hah
[Bm]Sons of [A]Hur the first[G]born
Of [D]Ephrathah the fa[A]ther of Bethle[D]hem
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
Gedor in the [G]hill country
[A]A name in the [D]line of Judah
A place in [G]the ancient land
[A]Where the genealogies [D]are drawn
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
Mered's wife bore Jered
[G]The father of Ge[A]dor
Son [Bm]of Bithiah [A]Pharaoh's daugh[G]ter
[D]In the [A]lineage of the [D]tribe
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}

{start_of_bridge: Bridge}
They [Bm]went to the entrance of Ge[F#m]dor
To [G]the east side of the [D]valley
[Bm]Looking for pasture for their [F#m]flocks
In the [G]quiet of the [A]hill
{end_of_bridge}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
Ge[D]dor in the hill [G]country
A name [A]in the line of [D]Judah
A place in the [G]ancient land
[A]Where the genealogies [D]are drawn
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Outro}
The land [G]was broad and [A]quiet
And [D]peaceful [A]for their [D]sheep
{end_of_verse}
